// Rule: [NO-MITRE-MAPPING] GTG-20006 - Actor Controlled Device Registration
// MITRE ATT&CK: NO-MITRE-MAPPING
// Classification: Validation query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Required telemetry: AuditLogs
// Purpose: Microsoft Sentinel validation for Entra audit coverage of a source-observed access maintenance behavior.
// Logic: Evaluate AuditLogs for actor controlled device registration using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result is not evidence of malicious activity.
// A match does not prove: successful exploitation, malicious ownership, downstream impact, campaign attribution or complete compromise without corroborating evidence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// GTG-20006 actor-controlled device registration
// Classification: Validation query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Entra audit logs exported to Log Analytics
// Objective: validate the tenant-specific audit representation of device registration.
// A result is not evidence of malicious activity.
// No threshold, rarity, join, parsing, or success-only filter is applied.

AuditLogs
| where OperationName in ("Add device", "Register device")
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    ActivityDateTime,
    Id,
    CorrelationId,
    OperationName,
    ActivityDisplayName,
    AADOperationType,
    LoggedByService,
    Identity,
    InitiatedBy,
    TargetResources,
    AdditionalDetails,
    Result,
    ResultType,
    ResultDescription
| order by TimeGenerated desc

